extends layout

include partials/footer

block content
  section.press
    .press__inner
      a.legal__home(href="/") ← Buried Worlds VR

      .press__head
        h1.h1 Press kit
        p.press__lede
          | Everything needed to write about Buried Worlds VR without emailing anyone
          | first. Screenshots, art and the trailer are free to use in coverage.

      .press__actions
        a.btn.btn--primary(href=`/press/${kitFile}` download) Download the kit · #{kitSize}
        a.btn.btn--secondary(href=links.metaQuestStoreCta + '?placement=press' target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-cta="press") Store page
        a.btn.btn--secondary(href=`mailto:${pressContact}`) #{pressContact}

      h2.legal__h Fact sheet
      .press-facts
        dl.press-facts__list
          div
            dt Title
            dd Buried Worlds VR
          div
            dt Store listing
            dd Titled #[em Buried Worlds] on the store — the same game
          div
            dt Platform
            dd #{product.store} — #{product.devices}
          div
            dt Price
            dd #{product.price} (Meta shows local currency by region)
          div
            dt Released
            dd #{product.releaseDateLabel}, in #{product.status}
          div
            dt Developer
            dd Cyril Gaillard, working alone
          div
            dt Studio
            dd #{product.publisher} (#{product.developer}), Victoria, Australia
          div
            dt Built with
            dd Unity 6, URP, OpenXR and the Meta XR SDK
          div
            dt Genres
            dd #{product.genres.join(', ')} · single player, no combat
          div
            dt Languages
            dd #{product.languages.join(' and ')}
          div
            dt Comfort
            dd #{product.comfort} · #{product.playModes} · teleport or free movement
          div
            dt Rating
            dd IARC #{product.ageRating}
          div
            dt Download size
            dd #{product.size}
          div
            dt Internet
            dd Not required once installed
          div
            dt Website
            dd
              a(href=siteUrl) buriedworlds.com

      h2.legal__h Descriptions
      p.press__note Take these as they are — no attribution needed, no need to reword.

      .press-copy
        span.press-copy__label One line
        p.press-copy__text= descriptions.oneLine

      .press-copy
        span.press-copy__label One paragraph
        p.press-copy__text= descriptions.short

      .press-copy
        span.press-copy__label Full description
        each para in descriptions.full
          p.press-copy__text= para

      h2.legal__h The five expeditions
      p.press__note
        | Every destination is a real place where treasure was actually found.
        | Each carries its in-game expedition name.
      .press-worlds
        each w in expeditions
          .press-world
            .press-world__head
              span.press-world__place= w.place
              span.press-world__region= w.region
            span.press-world__quest= w.questName
            p.press-world__blurb= w.blurb
            p.press-world__history= w.history

      h2.legal__h Getting the history right
      p.
        These are the details most worth checking before print, because they are
        the ones the game is built on and the ones an archaeologist or a
        detectorist will notice first.
      ul.legal__list
        li
          strong Hoxne, 1992.
          |  Eric Lawes was searching for a hammer lost by his tenant farmer,
          | Peter Whatling, when he found the hoard. The hammer was recovered as
          | well and is held with the hoard in the British Museum, Room 49. The
          | game recreates the hammer, and finding it is part of the expedition.
        li
          strong Coloma, January 1848.
          |  James Marshall's find at Sutter's Mill started the California Gold
          | Rush.
        li
          strong Carcassonne.
          |  The fortified city has been UNESCO-listed since 1997.
        li
          strong Bolonia.
          |  The ruins are the Roman town of Baelo Claudia, on the Andalusian
          | coast.
        li
          strong The detector's target ID scale.
          |  Gold and lead deliberately overlap on it, because that is what the
          | ground does to you in reality. Even the better detector cannot call
          | that one — which is the point.

      h2.legal__h The loop
      ol.press-loop
        each step in loop
          li
            strong= step[0]
            |  — #{step[1]}

      h2.legal__h What Early Access means here
      p.
        Five destinations are in the game today, along with the whole loop —
        detector, pickaxe, pan, sieve, magnet and brush. Kimberley, the Western
        Australian diamond country, is built and waiting as the first
        destination to arrive after launch. The full version is working toward
        twelve destinations and six languages, translated by people rather than
        by machine. There is a feedback screen inside the game that reaches the
        developer directly and does not ask who you are.

      h2.legal__h The developer
      p.
        Buried Worlds VR was built by Cyril Gaillard, alone, over roughly two
        years, trading as #{product.publisher} in Victoria, Australia. It started
        with a gold prospecting course in Maryborough, in the Victorian
        goldfields, which he never quite got over.
      p.
        The game is deliberately low-poly and flat-shaded so it holds frame rate
        on standalone hardware, which is why it runs on Quest 2 as well as the
        Quest 3 family rather than the newer headsets alone.

      h2.legal__h Screenshots
      p.press__note Click any image for the full 1920×1080 file.
      .press-shots
        each shot in screenshots
          figure.press-shot
            a(href=`/press/screenshots/${shot[0]}` target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer")
              img.press-shot__img(src=`/press/screenshots/${shot[0]}` alt=shot[1] loading="lazy" width="1920" height="1080")
            figcaption.press-shot__cap= shot[1]

      h2.legal__h Logo and art
      ul.press-files
        each item in art
          li
            a(href=`/press/${item[0]}` download)= item[1]
            span.press-files__meta= item[2]

      h2.legal__h Trailer
      p.
        Two minutes, no narration. It covers the loop and four of the five
        destinations.
      ul.press-files
        li
          a(href=trailer.full download) Launch trailer — 720p MP4
          span.press-files__meta 1280×720, 14 MB
      p.press__note
        | A 1080p master is available on request — ask at
        | #[a(href=`mailto:${pressContact}`) #{pressContact}].

      h2.legal__h Contact
      p.
        Press enquiries, review codes and interview requests go to
        #[a(href=`mailto:${pressContact}`) #{pressContact}]. Review codes are
        given with no conditions attached to what you say about the game.
      p.
        For anything less formal, the developer is on
        #[a(href=links.discord target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Discord]
        most days.

      h2.legal__h Using these assets
      p.
        The screenshots, key art, logo and trailer on this page may be used
        freely in reviews, previews, news coverage, videos and streams of
        Buried Worlds VR, including monetised ones. No permission needed and no
        need to ask first. Please do not alter the logo or present the artwork
        as your own work.

  +footer(links)
